; The OCaml live harness (F4.3): one explicitly named case per invocation, a
; gate variable that must be set, and per-adapter assertions rather than one
; generic "returned something" check.
;
; [seekwright-live] is built by [dune build @install] and is deliberately NOT
; part of the test aliases: [dune runtest] stays hermetic, and no gate step
; reaches a provider. Only the pure inventory and assertion tables are tested
; hermetically below — those tests dial nothing.
;
; The harness is manual/maintainer-only:
;   SEEKWRIGHT_LIVE_TESTS=1 seekwright-live freeserp
; A billed name is reachable only by naming it on a gated invocation; there is
; no "all configured providers" selector to sweep.
(executable
 (name main)
 (public_name seekwright-live)
 (package seekwright)
 (modules main)
 (libraries live_harness eio_main mirage-crypto-rng.unix unix))

(library
 (name live_harness)
 (modules cases checks runner)
 ; [seekwright.factory] is where the registry rows, the fetch stack and the app
 ; come from, so a live run exercises the application's own construction rather
 ; than a harness-only path. [eio] is the loop the grants are opened on; [unix]
 ; is the clock this one-shot process injects.
 (libraries seekwright seekwright.factory eio unix))

; Hermetic: the case table (17 provider names, 6 fetch cases, 2 agent depths),
; the selection rules — no all-providers spelling — the per-adapter assertion
; arms over synthetic responses, and the live-status consistency between the
; harness and the registry row. No socket, no key, no clock.
(test
 (name test_live_cases)
 (modules test_live_cases)
 (libraries live_harness seekwright.factory alcotest))
